# Revisions to skip when walking blame, one per line, newest last. Only
# whitespace-preserving reformats belong here: a commit listed below must not
# have changed a token, or blame will silently attribute real edits elsewhere.
#
# Squash is the only merge method the branch ruleset allows, so a reformat's
# revision does not exist until its own merge creates it, and an entry can only
# ever be written down afterwards. It must also name a merge that carried the
# reformat alone: a squashed commit that also changed a token would make blame
# skip that token's edit too.
#
# Configure a clone to honour this file once, with:
#
#     git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# GitHub's blame view reads it without being asked.

# Separate the definitions, break the templates, indent the lists at eight.
# Every C++ file it touched is byte-identical once whitespace is stripped. It
# also carries the .clang-format keys that produced the reformat, which cannot
# land in a separate merge: the keys alone would fail the clang-format gate,
# and the reformat alone would not match them.
